.history

# Python bytecode
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# pytest cache. Pytest writes a self-ignoring `.pytest_cache/.gitignore` containing `*`,
# so git already hides it — listed here so the dev tree does not depend on a generated
# file for that, and so `propagate.sh`/`retrofit.sh` have a matching named exclude.
.pytest_cache/

# Maintainer feedback-to-issues input (local triage only; it files GitHub issues, #49).
# The glob covers the numbered variants a multi-bootcamp triage round produces
# (…_01.md, …_13.md), not just the bare filename.
# Root-anchored on purpose: the transient working copy is ignored, while the processed
# archive under feedback/ IS tracked, so a raw report survives an overwrite.
/SENZING_BOOTCAMP_PLUGIN_FEEDBACK*.md
